@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option Desk - Prompt construction and the optional model boundary

actor "Caller" as caller
participant "Prompt builder" as prompts
participant "ArtifactStore" as store
participant "Optional summary model" as model
caller -> store : context_for(underlying)
store --> caller : saved artifact context
caller -> prompts : build_answer_prompt(extra_rules)
prompts -> prompts : system = REPORTING_RULES\n+ optional deployment rules
prompts --> caller : template with context and question
caller -> model : formatted system + human messages
model --> caller : summary text
note over prompts,model
Rules require artifact-grounded answers, degradation first,
correct units, visible missing values and model limitations.
These are prompt instructions, not a proof that every model obeys.
end note
note over caller,prompts
build_router_prompt() is a separate helper:
question -> proposed tool name and arguments.
The bounded graph does not call that router or let a model
choose its calculation stages. Its optional model summarizes.
end note

caption Sources: agent/src/optiondesk_agent/prompts.py and graph.py. A prompt helper does not execute a tool.
@enduml
